Consider:
struct Tnode {
	string word;
	int count;
	Tnode* left;
	Tnode* right;
};

Write a function for entering new words into a tree of Tnodes. Write a function
to write out a tree of Tnodes. Write a function to write out a tree of Tnodes
with the words in alphabetical order. Modify Tnode so that it stores (only) a
pointer to an arbitrary long word stored as an array of characters on free store
using new. Modify the functions to use the new definition of Tnode.
